  "body": "Stacked on #805 (ER collet chucks, itself on #800). Fork synced at v0.17.0.\n\n## What's in it\nTormach TTS holders in the built-in holder library (`crates/tools/src/holder_library_tts.rs`). They appear in the same `holder_library::library()` list the tool editor's picker shows and #799's MCP tool will read. No MCP tool is added here.\n\n- **TTS ER20** (default gauge 52 mm, Tormach's published installed height) and **TTS ER16** (49 mm). The nuts come from #792's single ER table: Ø35 and Ø32, no smaller than Tormach's published Ø34 and Ø27.\n- **TTS Weldon (set-screw) holders:** 1/4, 5/16, 3/8, 1/2 in and 6, 10, 12 mm. These are Tormach's TTS set-screw part numbers 31818-31824. No TTS 5/8 or 3/4 in set-screw holder was found: a 3/4 in tool takes the TTS collar, PN 32432, on its own shank.\n- **The TTS mount is a zero-standoff `Taper`** (`TTS`, `ring: \"collar\"`). The collar's top face is the gauge line: the shoulder seats on the spindle face, and Tormach's manual says every tool is measured from it. So **projection + gauge length = the collar-to-tip length the tool setter measures and the H offset holds.** The 3/4 in shank inside the R8 collet is not drawn, the same as a steep taper.\n- **Unpublished sizes are enveloped, larger never smaller:**\n  - collar Ø1.5 in × 0.5 in;\n  - set-screw body Ø1.5 in, plus #792's 1 mm screw allowance;\n  - 60 mm default set-screw gauge length.\n\n  Ø1.5 in is the TTS blank's machinable diameter.\n- `Taper` gains a `ring` field (\"flange\" or \"collar\"), so the picker line reads \"TTS collar Ø38.1 × 12.7\".\n- **Machine default: filed as #828, not built.** A `.mch` has no holder or spindle-mount field. Tormach's public mill comparison also shows the **770MX and 1100MX are BT30**, not TTS; TTS belongs to the 770M/1100M/PCNC/440. #828 proposes BT30 ER20 for the MX mills and TTS ER20 for the R8 mills.\n- The decision record is in `docs/decisions/794-tts-holders.md`.\n\n## Sources (dimensions and behaviour only)\n- Tormach TTS Operation Manual rev C, https://littlemachineshop.com/cdn/shop/files/TTSOperationManualRevC.pdf: the 3/4 in shank, the ground shoulder on the spindle face, and that tools are measured from the shoulder.\n- TTS ER20, PN 31829 (OD 34 mm, installed height 52 mm): https://tormach.com/tts-toolholder-er20-31829.html\n- TTS ER16, PN 31831 (OD 27 mm, installed height 49 mm): https://tormach.com/tts-toolholder-er16-31831.html\n- Set-screw holder part numbers:\n  - https://tormach.com/tts-set-screw-holder-31820-html.html\n  - TD10408: https://tormach.com/media/asset/t/d/td10408_tts_cnc_operators_set_0820a.pdf\n  - TD10416: https://tormach.com/media/asset/t/d/td10416_tts_basic_tooling_set_0120a.pdf\n- TTS blank, Ø1.5 in × 2.36 in machinable end: https://littlemachineshop.com/products/blank-tool-holder-tormach-tts\n- MX mills are BT30; PCNC and M mills are R8 + TTS: https://www.tormach.com/tormach_mills/\n\n## How tested\n- **camcraft-tools** (`holder_library::tts::tests`):\n  - `the_tts_table_is_the_recorded_one`: the published and enveloped numbers, the names and the default gauges.\n  - `the_tts_er20_outline_is_the_table`: point by point.\n  - `a_tts_set_screw_holder_steps_in_to_its_collar`\n  - `every_tts_profile_is_closed_and_tops_out_at_the_collar_face`: watertight and revolvable, with the gauge line as the top, at the default, a long and the minimum gauge.\n  - The existing `every_entry_draws_a_valid_profile_with_its_flange_and_nose` now covers TTS too.\n- **camcraft-app** (`tests/holder_library.rs`):\n  - `a_tts_holder_tops_out_at_the_collar_the_setter_measures_from`: gauge-length semantics through `SetToolBody::library` and `tool_body::judged`.\n  - `the_tts_er20_collar_strikes_a_wall_its_nut_misses`: a collision through the real fixture gate. The Ø38.1 collar hits a wall that a straight Ø35 body misses, and a wall at 20 mm is clear.\n- **camcraft-ui** (`egui_app::tests::tool_holder`, CWD `crates/ui`):\n  - `the_picker_lists_the_tts_holders_and_names_the_collar`: a structural test. It opens the Library holder list, the TTS entries are present, and a pick shows \"TTS collar Ø38.1\" and the 52 mm gauge.\n- **Local run:** the holder suites above pass. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-tools -p camcraft-app -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -D warnings` is clean.\n- **Linux quick gate** (`--base` #805's branch): result in a PR comment.\n- No snapshot PNG changes.\n\n## Not exercised\n**The real holders.** The maintainer's 770MX is BT30, so no real TTS holder was measured. A user with a TTS mill (770M, 1100M or PCNC), please measure and post:\n- the **collar OD** and **collar thickness** (shoulder face to where the body steps down);\n- the **ER20 nut OD** and length;\n- the **installed height** (collar face to nose face) of the ER20 and of one set-screw holder;\n- a set-screw holder's **body OD**.\n\nThe collar, set-screw body and set-screw gauge defaults are envelopes until then.\n\nChangelog: Built-in Tormach TTS holders (ER20, ER16 and 1/4-1/2 in / 6-12 mm set-screw) in the holder library, with the collar face as the gauge line the tool setter measures from.\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nFixes #794\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n",
